# cargo-fuzz working directories. The *working* corpus and the crash artefacts
# are local findings, not source: a crash worth keeping becomes a test in the
# crate it belongs to, which is where it will actually keep being run.
#
# `seeds/` is deliberately not here, and the difference is worth stating.
# A crash artefact is an output. A seed is an *input*: it is what stops a cold
# run spending its budget rediscovering that a lock file begins with
# `VEILLOK1`. See README.md for why only two targets have one.
target/
corpus/
artifacts/
coverage/
Cargo.lock
